  "question": {
    "text": "The interval in which the function $f(x)=x^x, x>0$, is strictly increasing is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "C2JOP",
      "text": "$\\left(0, \\frac{1}{e}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bJekV",
      "text": "$(0, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QNFuz",
      "text": "$\\left.\\left[\\frac{1}{e}, \\infty\\right)\\right]_V$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "5tbqs",
      "text": "$\\left[\\frac{1}{e^2}, 1\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{x}^{\\mathrm{x}} ; \\mathrm{x}>0 \\\\\n& \\ell \\operatorname{nn}=\\mathrm{x} \\ell \\mathrm{n} \\mathrm{x} \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{y}} \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{x}}+\\ln \\mathrm{n} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\mathrm{x}^{\\mathrm{x}}(1+\\ell \\mathrm{n} x)\n\\end{aligned}$\nfor strictly increasing\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d y}{d x} \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow x^x(1+\\ell n x) \\geq 0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\ell n x \\geq-1\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & x \\geq e^{-1} \\\\ & x \\geq \\frac{1}{e} \\\\ & x \\in\\left[\\frac{1}{e}, \\infty\\right)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
